---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../site.config';
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="What Sink Alike stores and why.">
  <div class="wrap narrow">
    <header class="page-head">
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p>The short version: we store as little as possible and never sell or share it.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What we store</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>If you comment or vote without an account</strong>, we store your comment, the name you typed (if any), and a
        one-way hash of your IP address so we can stop spam and double-voting. We can’t turn that hash back into your IP address.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>If you sign in</strong> (Google, email or phone), we store your name, your email address or phone number, your
        profile picture if Google provides one, and a login session. Your email and phone number are never shown publicly.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>On your device</strong>, the site remembers your theme choice and where you got to in each episode. That data
        never leaves your browser.
      </p>
      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>We use Cloudflare Web Analytics, which counts page views without cookies or tracking you across sites.</p>
      <p>
        We also count a few things people do here, like playing an episode, how far into it they listen, clicking a
        “Listen on” or sponsor link, and what they search for in quotes. Each count records the page, your country and whether
        you’re on a phone or computer, never who you are: no cookies, no IP address and no account details.
      </p>
      <h2>Audio</h2>
      <p>Episodes stream from our podcast host (Spotify for Creators), which has its own privacy policy.</p>
      <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
      <p>
        You can delete your account and every comment you’ve posted from your <a href="/account/">account page</a>. For anything
        else, email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
